%% ContextFrame -> cognition/agents -> Proposal -> validation -> policy -> execution.
%% See ../COGNITION_MODEL.md and ../MK42_ARCHITECTURE.md §8.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as Perception
    participant CTX as Context Compiler (Kernel)
    participant WM as World Model
    participant MEM as Memory
    participant COG as Cognition / Agent (no creds, no effects)
    participant GW as Model Gateway (holds provider keys)
    participant VAL as Validator
    participant POL as Policy Engine (deterministic)
    participant PERM as Permission Engine
    participant EXE as Capability Executor
    participant AD as Adapter (out-of-process, scoped cred)

    P->>CTX: Observation events (signal)
    CTX->>WM: time-scoped fact query (+ freshness hint)
    CTX->>MEM: top-k recall (relevance floor)
    Note over CTX: fill ContextFrame by priority tiers,\nstop at context-unit budget, mark unknowns + truncation
    CTX->>COG: ContextFrame
    COG->>GW: ModelRequest (provider-neutral, locality constraint)
    GW-->>COG: ModelResponse
    COG->>VAL: Proposal (untrusted; may be derivedFromUntrusted)
    VAL->>POL: validated proposal + resolved riskClass
    POL-->>EXE: ALLOW | DENY | REQUIRE_APPROVAL
    Note over POL: LLM PolicyRecommendation may be ONE input,\nnever the verdict (L21)
    EXE->>PERM: acquire authority for requiredScopes
    PERM-->>EXE: scoped TTL authority token
    EXE->>EXE: freshness barrier (re-read grant) + capability.started
    EXE->>EXE: simulate if riskClass >= HIGH (dry-run cred) -> approval
    EXE->>AD: execute
    AD-->>EXE: raw result
    EXE->>EXE: verify effect against the world (mandatory)
    EXE-->>WM: emit capability.verified + derived facts (epistemicStatus: observed)
    EXE-->>COG: outcome for follow-up planning
